{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.QBetaPerBlockChiClosedForms"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_explicit_has_q2_minus_1_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_explicit_has_q2_minus_1_factor","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance.lean#L222-L242","doc":"**Theorem (explicit-instance (q²−1) factor).** For `q > 0`, the\ncanonical Δτ_M at the explicit instance factors through `(q² − 1)`, so it\nvanishes at the classical point `q = 1` for the structural reason (the\n`(q²−1)` factor in every per-block character), independently of the\n`√q`-bearing weights.\n\nProof: unfold to the `z`-weighted block sum\n(`delta_tau_M_canonical_explicit_eq`), substitute the per-block\nfactorisations from `chi_blocks_have_q2_minus_1_factor`, and pull out the\ncommon `(q²−1)`; the cofactor carries the weights `z = markov_parameter q`\nas an opaque atom under `ring`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_explicit_vanish_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_explicit_vanish_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance.lean#L214-L220","doc":"**Theorem (explicit-instance vanishing at q = 1).** The canonical Δτ_M\nat the explicit instance vanishes at the classical point. This is the\nconditional `delta_tau_M_canonical_vanish_at_one` dispatched at the\nexplicit instance — confirming the conditional theorem is non-vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_explicit_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_explicit_eq","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance.lean#L200-L212","doc":"**Lemma (explicit-instance unfolding).** With the explicit √q-bearing\ninstance, the canonical Δτ_M is the concrete `z`-weighted block sum, where\n`z = markov_parameter q = √q / (1 + q)`:\n\n  `Δτ_M^can(q) = z · χ_(3) + (1/2 − z) · χ_(2,1) + z · χ_(1,1,1)`.\n\nPure definitional unfolding (the instance projections β/ι-reduce). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.is_inhabited","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.is_inhabited","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance.lean#L181-L187","doc":"**Witness (sanity check): the class is inhabited.** This is\nsyntactic; it confirms that subsequent conditional theorems\n`[CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3]` have at least one concrete dispatch\ntarget. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_two_block_normalisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_two_block_normalisation","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance.lean#L172-L179","doc":"**The two nonzero canonical weights sum with their dimensions to one**,\nwith the `(1³)` block contributing nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_at_canonical_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_at_canonical_eq","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance.lean#L163-L170","doc":"**Δτ_M at the canonical instance**, unfolded to the `𝔰𝔩₂`-weighted block\nsum with the `(1³)` block dropping out by the row bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_resolves_to_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.delta_tau_M_canonical_resolves_to_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance.lean#L147-L161","doc":"**Resolution guard: the default instance IS the canonical one.**\n\nThe left side elaborates by instance resolution; the right names\n`canonicalInstance` explicitly.  They are `rfl`-equal only because\nresolution picks the canonical weights — if a second `instance` of the\nclass were ever declared, or `explicitInstance` promoted back, this would\nstop typechecking rather than silently changing what every bare\n`delta_tau_M_canonical q` means.\n\nVerified to have teeth: the same statement written against\n`explicitInstance` does *not* typecheck. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_is_inhabitant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_is_inhabitant","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance.lean#L140-L145","doc":"**The canonical weight set is a genuine inhabitant of the class**, so the\n`[CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3]`-conditional theorems are non-vacuous at the\nweights the production trace actually carries — not only at the\n`√q`-bearing `explicitInstance`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_y111_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_y111_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance.lean#L135-L138","doc":"**The `(1³)` block carries zero weight** at the canonical instance —\nthe `𝔰𝔩₂` row bound, stated where downstream consumers can use it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.canonicalInstance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.canonicalInstance","kind":"instance","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance.lean#L103-L133","doc":"**The canonical inhabitant of `CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3`.**\n\nThe `𝔰𝔩₂` quantum dimensions of the production trace.  Unlike\n`explicitInstance`, this is not merely *an* inhabitant: it is the one the\nconvention-D Markov trace actually carries, derived from the framing\nratio rather than chosen to satisfy the normalisation.\n\nThe normalisation is an identity rather than a constraint that had to be\narranged: `(q⁴+1) + 2q² = (q²+1)²`.\n\n**This is the class's default instance** (owner decision, 2026-09-03, bean\n`qou-6u92`).  Bare `delta_tau_M_canonical q` therefore means the production\ntrace's Δτ_M, not the `√q`-bearing toy.\n\nThe promotion was made as a PAIR with demoting `explicitInstance` to a `def`\nbelow, and the pairing is the point: two global instances of one class is a\nsilent hazard, because resolution takes the later declaration and nothing in\nthe source says so.  With exactly one instance, what a bare use means is\nstated rather than inferred.  Verified by `lean`-direct on all five files that\nmention the class, against a green baseline taken before the change. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_y21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_y21","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance.lean#L100-L101","doc":"The canonical weight on `V_(2,1)`: `1/[2]_q² = q²/(q²+1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_y3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.canonical_y3","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance.lean#L97-L98","doc":"The canonical weight on `V_(3)`: `[4]_q/[2]_q³ = (q⁴+1)/(q²+1)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.explicitInstance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3.explicitInstance","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/QBetaCanonicalMarkovWeightsInstance.lean#L34-L62","doc":"**Explicit √q-bearing instance of `CanonicalMarkovWeightsH3`.**\n\nConstructed from the Markov parameter `z(q) = √q / (1 + q)`. The\nsum-of-dimensions normalisation `y_(3) + 2·y_(2,1) + y_(1,1,1) = 1`\nfollows from `z + (1 - 2z) + z = 1` for any real-valued z.\n\n**Not canonical.** This is one valid inhabitant of the class — it\nsatisfies the normalisation because `z + 2(1/2 - z) + z = 1` holds for\n*any* `z`, which is precisely why it inhabits the class without being\nthe production weights.  ~~identifying THE canonical inhabitant is open\nmath~~ — that is now `canonicalInstance` below (2026-09-03).\n\n⚠ **Demoted from `instance` to `def` (2026-09-03).**  It remains a\nfirst-class inhabitant and every use of it below is unchanged: they all\nname it explicitly with `@`, and `is_inhabited` names it too.  What\nchanges is only that it is no longer a candidate for *implicit*\nresolution, so a bare `delta_tau_M_canonical q` now unambiguously means\nthe canonical weights rather than whichever instance was declared last. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:qbeta-canonical-markov-weights-explicit-instance","label":"prop:qbeta-canonical-markov-weights-explicit-instance","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/qbeta-canonical-markov-weights-explicit-instance.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}